0..61 Comment "/// This source compares a defined composite with `Path.step`"
62..85 Comment "/// at stuck endpoints."
86..89 Comment "///"
90..131 Comment "/// The `concat` body is `Path.step p q`."
132..190 Comment "/// A held call can supply an endpoint to either spelling."
191..194 Comment "///"
195..254 Comment "/// The machine evaluates the call where the type reads it."
255..303 Comment "/// The kernel repeats that endpoint comparison."
304..376 Comment "/// At a stuck call, the type of `concat` reads the endpoint through the"
377..454 Comment "/// environment that its call binds. The type written with `Path.step` writes"
455..477 Comment "/// the call in place."
478..481 Comment "///"
482..518 Comment "/// - see: #4038 — stuck endpoints"
519..558 Comment "/// - see: #4005 — returned endpoints"
559..599 Comment "/// - see: #4011 — bind over transport"
601..646 Comment "/// The `concat` function composes two paths."
